Apple today announced "Audio Intelligence," a new suite of Apple Intelligence-powered features for the Apple Watch Series 12 and Apple Watch Ultra 4 that use the built-in microphone to help users catch missed moments in conversation and stay aware of important sounds.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/apple-watch-series-12.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063371" /><br/>
The Apple Watch's Audio Intelligence comprises four features:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>Siri Recap</strong>: Uses ambient listening to generate high-level notes from conversations, such as takeaways from a team meeting or a parent-teacher conference, producing an Apple Intelligence-generated title, summary, and key points reviewable in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> app.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Live Rewind</strong>: Lets users "go back in time for 15 seconds," transcribing and displaying what was just said in a conversation with a double press of the Digital Crown.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Shazam</strong>: Automatically identifies music playing nearby and surfaces the song title and artist on the Music Recognition widget in the Smart Stack.</li> <br/>
<li><strong>Sound Recognition</strong>: Brings sound alerts to Apple Watch for users who are deaf or hard of hearing, listening for sirens, alarms, doorbells, a baby crying, and more, even when their iPhone isn't nearby.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
Apple emphasized that &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Recap is opt-in and configurable, telling users they "control if and when &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Recap takes notes." Users can set it to always listen or schedule it for specific contexts, such as only at work or never at night, and can toggle it on or off at any time from Control Center. Apple reiterated that none of the Audio Intelligence features create or store audio recordings, with raw audio processed in an isolated Secure Exclave on the S11 chip and deleted immediately after use.<br/>
<br/>
Audio Intelligence and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI both require an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone, with Live Rewind and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Recap limited to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-16/">iPhone 16</a> or later (excluding the iPhone 16e).<br/>
<br/>
